  "answer_text": "Here's some information about **\"Still in Love with You\"** by **Brooks & Dunn**:\n\n- **\"Still in Love with You\"** is a **1991 song** by Brooks & Dunn, from their album **Brand New Man**.\n\n- It is the **tenth track** on *Brand New Man*.\n\nThe song is a classic country heartbreak ballad. It tells the story of someone who has to say goodbye to a loved one but can't shake their feelings \u2014 no matter how far they go, they'd still wake up in love. The iconic chorus features the lines: *\"If I had a horse, I'd ride off in the sunset / If I had wings, I'd fly off in the sky so blue / If I had the time, I'd spend my whole life dreaming / But I'd wake up still in love with you.\"*\n\n**Album:** *Brand New Man* (1991)\n**Artist:** Brooks & Dunn (Kix Brooks & Ronnie Dunn)\n**Genre:** Country\n\nYou can listen to it on [Spotify](https://open.spotify.com/track/5nTh5z1Uac2istxVmX3qH8) or watch it on [YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Iyk_dM9CbUY). \ud83c\udfb5",
